      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:2:3:131:7",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/3/131/7",
      "text": [
        " رِوَايَةِ سُلَيْمَانَ بْنِ دَاوُدَ اَلْمِنْقَرِيِّ عَنْ سُفْيَانَ بْنِ عُيَيْنَةَ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : فِي قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ «فَمَنْ تَعَجَّلَ فِي يَوْمَيْنِ فَلاٰ إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ» «يَعْنِي مَنْ مَاتَ فَلاَ إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ «وَ مَنْ تَأَخَّرَ» أَجَلُهُ «فَلاٰ إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ لِمَنِ اِتَّقىٰ» اَلْكَبَائِرَ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3021 - In a narration from Sulaiman ibn Dawood al-Minqari, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Abu Abdullah (as), regarding the verse of Allah (swt), the Exalted:\n\"So whoever hastens [to leave] in two days - there is no sin upon him; and whoever delays - there is no sin upon him for one who fears [Allah (swt)]\" (Surah Al-Baqarah 2:203):\nImam (as) said: \"This means: whoever dies [after completing Hajj], there is no sin upon him. And for whoever's term is delayed, there is no sin upon him as long as they avoid major sins.\""
        ]
      }
